# Ensure shell scripts use LF so they run in Linux containers.
# Broader *.sh rule prevents CRLF regressions when new scripts are added
# (e.g. on Windows checkouts with autocrlf=true).
*.sh text eol=lf
services/dashboard/dashboard/entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
scripts/llamacpp/run-llama-server.sh text eol=lf
# nginx config is COPYed into the codebase-memory-ui image; keep LF so nginx
# doesn't choke on CRLF after a Windows checkout.
services/codebase-memory-ui/nginx.conf text eol=lf
# The agent image's whole build context is LF: `docker build` copies the working tree as checked
# out, so a CRLF wrapper ships a CR-terminated shebang that is "not found" (github-app-token,
# 2026-10-15), patches stop applying, and spliced skill markdown mixes endings. One rule for the
# directory, so a new file is covered without an edit here (tests/test_image_contexts_lf.py).
services/hermes/** text=auto eol=lf

# Bind-mounted into Linux containers as an executable (the trainer venv-python
# lease seam) — a CRLF shebang (`python3\r`) breaks exec on Windows checkouts.
assets/* text eol=lf

# YAML manifests are LF always — agents editing from Windows-adjacent runtimes kept
# committing CRLF rewrites that turned 3-line pin bumps into 358-line diffs (PR #154).
# `text eol=lf` makes git normalize on checkin AND checkout, ending the class.
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf

# JSON catalogs/fixtures are the same class: PR #415 committed five of them CRLF from a
# Windows-side edit, inflating the rename diff (one catalog showed as 67%-similar, another
# as add+delete) until manually converted. `text eol=lf` normalizes checkin AND checkout.
*.json text eol=lf

# Frontend test JS/JSX hit the same class on the #415 approval (two test files committed CRLF
# from a Windows-side edit, showing as whole-file rewrites); normalize them like the other text.
*.js text eol=lf
*.jsx text eol=lf

# Patch files are COPYed into Linux image builds and fed to `git apply` — a CRLF
# checkout on Windows (autocrlf=true) hands the builder a patch whose hunks no
# longer byte-match the LF upstream sources. Keep them LF on both directions.
*.diff text eol=lf
*.patch text eol=lf

# The patched llama.cpp Dockerfile carries a python heredoc (PATCH 1) that is fed verbatim to the
# Linux builder; keep the whole build context LF so a Windows checkout cannot alter what it runs.
services/llamacpp-patched/** text eol=lf

# The NInfer Dockerfile is fed to a Linux builder; keep its context LF like the patched llama.cpp one.
services/ninfer/** text eol=lf
